# Tracks awesomeWM upstream master, NOT the v4.3 tag the stable "awesome"
# package builds from. v4.3 is from January 2019 - this commit is ~1745
# commits and 7+ years past it, so nothing about the stable template's
# dependency list was assumed to still be correct; every entry below was
# re-derived directly from this commit's awesomeConfig.cmake, not copied
# from the stable template. Concretely different from stable v4.3:
#
#   - glib-2.0 (>=2.79.2) is now a hard REQUIRED dependency
#     (pkg_check_modules(AWESOME_REQUIRED REQUIRED ...) includes it) -
#     absent from the v4.3 template entirely. Without glib-devel here
#     the cmake configure step fails outright.
#   - pango is GONE. Grepped every .c/.h file and both CMakeLists.txt/
#     awesomeConfig.cmake in this commit - zero references anywhere.
#     Including pango-devel here would just be dead weight from having
#     assumed the stable template's list still applied.
#   - xcb-util-errors-devel added (WITH_XCB_ERRORS autoOption - not
#     required, but small and gives much more readable X11 error
#     messages when enabled, so included by default like the small
#     optional deps in the other templates in this repo).
#   - the LuaJIT build_option from the stable template was intentionally
#     NOT carried over: it depends on `vsed`-patching two exact lines
#     in awesomeConfig.cmake/tests/examples/CMakeLists.txt
#     ("COMMAND lua\b" / "LUA_COV_RUNNER lua\b") that no longer exist in
#     this commit (the test-runner invocation was refactored to
#     shebang'd executable .lua scripts). Blindly copying the sed would
#     either silently no-op or break given a different current
#     structure I did not fully re-verify - dropped rather than guess.
#     Standard (non-JIT) lua53 path only, for now.
#
# xcb-randr/xcb-xtest/xcb-xinerama/xcb-shape/xcb-xfixes/xcb-xkb (all
# pkg_check_modules'd individually in awesomeConfig.cmake) all come from
# the single upstream libxcb source tree Void's libxcb-devel is built
# from - confirmed via its template, not assumed.
#
# VERSION handling: awesomeConfig.cmake computes VERSION via `git
# describe --dirty` when `${SOURCE_DIR}/.git` exists, else reads
# `.version_stamp` (only present in awesomewm's own dist.sh-built
# release tarballs, not a plain GitHub commit archive like this one),
# else falls back to the literal string "devel". Since neither .git nor
# .version_stamp exist in this tarball, -DOVERRIDE_VERSION is required
# or `awesome --version` silently reports "devel". _describe was
# computed for real via `git describe --tags` against this exact commit
# (not guessed/hand-assembled) after unshallowing history back past the
# v4.3 tag. xbps' own version= field can't contain dashes, hence the
# separate ${version}=4.3.1745 (base tag + `git rev-list v4.3..HEAD
# --count`) used for package versioning/comparison, independent of the
# richer string baked into the actual awesome binary via OVERRIDE_VERSION.
#
# replaces/provides mirror void-packages' own convention for -git
# variants shadowing a stable package (see monsterwm-git): can't have
# both "awesome" and "awesome-git" installed at once, since they
# install the same files.

CFLAGS="-fcommon"

post_patch() {
	sed -i '/add_dependencies.*check-examples/d' CMakeLists.txt
}

post_install() {
	vlicense LICENSE
}
